# Citation File Format 1.2.0. GitHub reads this to offer "Cite this
# repository", and Zenodo reads it when archiving a release.
#
# UPDATE `version` AND `date-released` BEFORE TAGGING A RELEASE. They are the
# two fields that go stale silently, and tests/testthat/test-metadata.R holds
# `version` to DESCRIPTION so that half cannot drift unnoticed.
#
# This file and .zenodo.json are excluded from the package tarball via
# .Rbuildignore: CRAN flags non-standard top-level files.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "staleness: Apply and Calibrate Published Signals for Updating Meta-Analyses"
abstract: >-
  Applies the five published statistical methods for detecting whether a
  systematic review or meta-analysis has gone out of date, and provides a
  backtesting engine to calibrate those methods against historical evidence.
  Two of the five depart from their sources where the published procedure
  could not be reproduced as stated; every departure is measured and
  documented. The package performs no literature searching and no screening.
authors:
  - family-names: "Núñez"
    given-names: "Javier"
    email: "jnverbel@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-09"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jnverbel/staleness"
url: "https://github.com/jnverbel/staleness"
keywords:
  - meta-analysis
  - systematic-review
  - evidence-synthesis
  - research-synthesis
  - reproducibility
  - r
references:
  - type: article
    title: "How quickly do systematic reviews go out of date? A survival analysis"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Shojania"
        given-names: "Kaveh G."
    year: 2007
    doi: "10.7326/0003-4819-147-4-200708210-00179"
    notes: "Source of the Ottawa method, and of the survival estimates this package's motivation rests on."
  - type: article
    title: "Comparison of statistical methods used to detect the need for updating systematic reviews"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Pattanittum"
        given-names: "Porjai"
    year: 2012
    doi: "10.1371/journal.pone.0048894"
    notes: "The only published comparison running all five detectors side by side; its Appendix S3 is a test fixture here."
